docs {
  # List Mutual Groups

  **Method:** `GET`
  **Endpoint:** `/api/v1/friendships/:id/mutual-groups`
  **Auth:** Required

  ## Description

  Lists groups that both participants of an accepted friendship belong to. Either participant can make this request with an active account. Set `friendshipId` manually in the selected Local environment using the selected item's `friendship_id` from List Friends.

  This endpoint follows the same membership rules as `mutual_group_count` in List Friends. A group is included when both memberships are `ACTIVE` and neither member has left. Non-deleted groups in all three states, `ACTIVE`, `SETTLING`, and `CLOSED`, are included. Results are ordered by group ID descending.

  ## Request

  ### Headers

  | Field | Type | Required | Description |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `Authorization` | string | Yes | Bearer access token of either friendship participant |

  ### Path Parameters

  | Field | Type | Required | Description |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `id` | integer | Yes | Positive friendship ID from List Friends |

  ### Query Parameters

  | Field | Type | Required | Description |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `page` | integer | No | Starts at 1. Defaults to 1. |
  | `limit` | integer | No | From 1 to 100. Defaults to 20. |

  No request body is required. Empty query values use their defaults. Invalid numbers or an overflowing pagination offset return `400 BAD_REQUEST`.

  ## Response

  **`200 OK`**

  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "data": {
      "items": [
        {
          "id": 12,
          "title": "Weekend trip",
          "cover_url": "https://storage.example.com/group-covers/weekend-trip.png?signature=example",
          "member_count": 5
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "title": "Dinner plans",
          "cover_url": null,
          "member_count": 3
        }
      ],
      "pagination": {
        "page": 1,
        "limit": 20,
        "total": 2
      }
    }
  }
  ```

  | Field | Meaning |
  | --- | --- |
  | `data.items[].id` | Group ID used to open the group. |
  | `data.items[].title` | Current group title. |
  | `data.items[].cover_url` | Temporary URL for the cover image. Use a placeholder if null. This can happen when there is no cover, access is unavailable, or storage cannot generate a URL. |
  | `data.items[].member_count` | Number of active members who have not left this group. |
  | `data.pagination.total` | Number of matching groups before pagination. |

  When there are no shared groups, the response contains `items: []` and `total: 0`. A page beyond the available results also contains `items: []` and keeps the matching total.

  ## Errors

  | HTTP | code | error | When |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | 400 | `BAD_REQUEST` | `bad request payload or parameters` | Invalid friendship ID, page, limit, or pagination offset. |
  | 401 | `MISSING_TOKEN` | `authorization token is missing` | The Bearer access token is missing. |
  | 401 | `TOKEN_INVALID` | `authorization token is invalid` | The token is invalid or is a refresh token. |
  | 401 | `TOKEN_EXPIRED` | `authorization token has expired` | The token has expired. |
  | 401 | `TOKEN_REVOKED` | `authorization token has been revoked` | The token has been blacklisted. |
  | 403 | `USER_INACTIVE` | `user account is deactivated` | The authenticated account is inactive. |
  | 403 | `FRIENDSHIP_FORBIDDEN` | `you are not allowed to perform this friendship operation` | The caller does not participate in this friendship. |
  | 404 | `USER_NOT_FOUND` | `user not found` | The caller's account is missing or soft-deleted. |
  | 404 | `FRIENDSHIP_NOT_FOUND` | `friendship not found` | The friendship is missing or soft-deleted. |
  | 409 | `FRIENDSHIP_INVALID_STATUS` | `friendship status does not allow this operation` | The caller participates in a pending or rejected relationship. |
  | 500 | `INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR` | `an internal server error occurred` | An internal dependency or database operation failed. |

  **Example: 403 Forbidden**

  ```json
  {
    "success": false,
    "code": "FRIENDSHIP_FORBIDDEN",
    "error": "you are not allowed to perform this friendship operation"
  }
  ```
}
